| clean reference -- confirmed clean by the user this session).
| This source has NO anonymous KLayout-style "$N" nets: every
| node is a real port name (P1..P15/VDD/VSS) or a real synthesis
| net name (e.g. bit_cnt[0], _065_).
| VDD/GND supply nodes (VDD/VSS pre-rename) are
| renamed literally "Vdd"/"Gnd" -- IRSIM looks for those exact
| names by default (design_notes.md 76.8).
| BUFTH (scl/sda_in Schmitt-trigger input buffer) is substituted
| with BUF_X1 (plain 2-stage inverter, identical pin list) --
| BUFTH's regenerative feedback is unresolvable by IRSIM's ternary
| switch-level solver on every transition, not just cold start
| (design_notes.md 76.12-76.15).
| The old gen_irsim_sim.py's insert_sda_hiz_inverter() compensating
| fix is deliberately NOT applied here: it worked around a v7-era
| sda_oe/HIZ13 RTL polarity bug that was fixed at the RTL source for
| V8+ (see README.md); this source's schematic already reflects
| that corrected RTL.
